```plaintext
0result.sql
```

Reason  
• 0result.sql correctly filters out null user‑ids, guaranteeing that an anonymous (NULL) bucket cannot accidentally become the “top user”.  
• 2result.sql is missing this filter, so a NULL group could outrank real users.  
• 1result.sql is also correct but its secondary sort key uses the original column alias (“user”) instead of the selected alias (“user_id”), which may confuse readability. 0result.sql keeps the naming consistent (`user_id`).